async_generator_misuse.vlt:57:19: error: `AsyncGenerator` cannot be extended
use composition instead: a class with a `AsyncGenerator` field
async_generator_misuse.vlt:27:30: error: an async generator must return `AsyncGenerator<T>`, `AsyncIterator<T>` or `AsyncIterable<T>`, found the sync `Generator<i64, never>`
drop `async`, or declare the result as `AsyncGenerator<T>`
async_generator_misuse.vlt:31:25: error: a generator must return `Generator<T>`, `Iterator<T>` or `Iterable<T>`, found the async `AsyncGenerator<i64, never>`
make it an async generator: `async function*` (methods: `async *name()`)
async_generator_misuse.vlt:35:17: error: an async generator must declare its return type
write `AsyncGenerator<T>`, where `T` is the type of the values it yields
async_generator_misuse.vlt:10:3: error: `for await` is only allowed inside async functions
mark the enclosing function or arrow `async`
async_generator_misuse.vlt:16:3: error: `for await` is not allowed in a generator
make it an async generator (`async function*`, methods: `async *name()`), whose body can await
async_generator_misuse.vlt:22:19: error: cannot iterate over a value of type `AsyncGenerator<i64, never>`
`for...of` works on arrays (`T[]`), on `Map`s and classes with an `entries()` method, and on iterables: values with a `[Symbol.iterator]()` method (`implements Iterable<T>`)
`AsyncGenerator<i64, never>` is an async iterable: iterate it with `for await (const x of ...)` in an async function
async_generator_misuse.vlt:40:10: error: a generator cannot return a value
`return;` ends the generator; to produce a last value, `yield` it before returning
async_generator_misuse.vlt:47:5: error: `yield` cannot be used in a `finally` block
a `finally` block also runs when the generator is closed early (`return()`, or dropping it), where it cannot pause: move the `yield` out of the `finally`
async_generator_misuse.vlt:73:25: error: cannot iterate over a value of type `i64`
`for await` works on async iterables: values with a `[Symbol.asyncIterator]()` method (`implements AsyncIterable<T>`, async generators), and on what `for...of` takes (arrays, iterables), awaiting promise elements
async_generator_misuse.vlt:76:25: error: `[Symbol.asyncIterator]()` must return an `AsyncIterator<T>`, found `i64[]`
declare the iterator class with `implements AsyncIterator<T>` and an `async next(): Promise<IteratorResult<T>>` method, or return `AsyncIterator<T>`
async_generator_misuse.vlt:80:25: error: cannot iterate over a `Record<string, i64>` with `for...of`
iterate its keys with `for (const k of Object.keys(rec))` or its entries with `for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(rec))`
async_generator_misuse.vlt:83:13: error: generators cannot be created with `new`
write an async generator function (`async function* f(): AsyncGenerator<T> { ... }`) and call it
async_generator_misuse.vlt:67:25: error: `consume` throws `Read`, which its `throws` clause does not allow
add `Read` to the `throws` clause, or catch it
